{
  "total": 581.281,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "S01",
      "start": 0.4,
      "speech_end": 1.6,
      "end": 2.4,
      "dur": 2.0,
      "text": "You own your phone."
    },
    {
      "id": "S02",
      "start": 2.4,
      "speech_end": 6.39,
      "end": 7.19,
      "dur": 4.79,
      "text": "You paid for it. It's yours. It's in your pocket right now."
    },
    {
      "id": "S03",
      "start": 7.19,
      "speech_end": 10.03,
      "end": 10.83,
      "dur": 3.64,
      "text": "And Apple decides what is allowed to run on it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S04",
      "start": 10.83,
      "speech_end": 18.53,
      "end": 19.33,
      "dur": 8.5,
      "text": "Not just software that's dangerous. Not just software that's broken. Software Apple hasn't put its stamp on."
    },
    {
      "id": "S05",
      "start": 19.33,
      "speech_end": 23.68,
      "end": 24.48,
      "dur": 5.15,
      "text": "That is not a complaint about quality. The phone is superb."
    },
    {
      "id": "S06",
      "start": 24.48,
      "speech_end": 27.17,
      "end": 29.77,
      "dur": 5.29,
      "text": "It's a question about who the thing belongs to."
    },
    {
      "id": "S07",
      "start": 29.77,
      "speech_end": 32.93,
      "end": 34.53,
      "dur": 4.76,
      "text": "And once you notice it, you start seeing it everywhere."
    },
    {
      "id": "S07b",
      "start": 34.53,
      "speech_end": 37.54,
      "end": 39.54,
      "dur": 5.01,
      "text": "And it's why some people can't stand this company."
    },
    {
      "id": "S08",
      "start": 39.54,
      "speech_end": 44.23,
      "end": 45.03,
      "dur": 5.49,
      "text": "In 2016, the iPhone 7 arrived without a headphone socket."
    },
    {
      "id": "S09",
      "start": 45.03,
      "speech_end": 48.315,
      "end": 49.115,
      "dur": 4.085,
      "text": "The plug it dropped had been standard since the 1960s."
    },
    {
      "id": "S09b",
      "start": 49.115,
      "speech_end": 52.975,
      "end": 53.775,
      "dur": 4.66,
      "text": "Stereos. Aeroplane armrests. Almost every phone in the shop."
    },
    {
      "id": "S10",
      "start": 53.775,
      "speech_end": 56.405,
      "end": 57.205,
      "dur": 3.43,
      "text": "Apple went on stage and gave a reason."
    },
    {
      "id": "S10b",
      "start": 57.205,
      "speech_end": 58.293,
      "end": 60.493,
      "dur": 3.288,
      "text": "Courage."
    },
    {
      "id": "S11",
      "start": 60.493,
      "speech_end": 63.243,
      "end": 64.043,
      "dur": 3.55,
      "text": "That isn't a reason. It's a slogan."
    },
    {
      "id": "S12",
      "start": 64.043,
      "speech_end": 65.812,
      "end": 66.612,
      "dur": 2.569,
      "text": "And Apple was right anyway."
    },
    {
      "id": "S12b",
      "start": 66.612,
      "speech_end": 73.432,
      "end": 74.232,
      "dur": 7.62,
      "text": "Three months before that phone went on sale, wireless headphones had already passed wired ones in American shops."
    },
    {
      "id": "S12c",
      "start": 74.232,
      "speech_end": 78.292,
      "end": 80.692,
      "dur": 6.46,
      "text": "Not by how many sold. By how much people spent on them."
    },
    {
      "id": "S13",
      "start": 80.692,
      "speech_end": 85.932,
      "end": 88.532,
      "dur": 7.84,
      "text": "Being told what you need, and then discovering you did need it, is a very particular feeling."
    },
    {
      "id": "S14",
      "start": 88.532,
      "speech_end": 90.212,
      "end": 91.012,
      "dur": 2.48,
      "text": "And it wasn't the only port."
    },
    {
      "id": "S15",
      "start": 91.012,
      "speech_end": 96.852,
      "end": 97.652,
      "dur": 6.64,
      "text": "In 2012, Apple replaced the connector on the bottom of the iPhone with one of its own design."
    },
    {
      "id": "S16",
      "start": 97.652,
      "speech_end": 99.612,
      "end": 100.412,
      "dur": 2.76,
      "text": "It kept it for eleven years."
    },
    {
      "id": "S17",
      "start": 100.412,
      "speech_end": 104.502,
      "end": 105.302,
      "dur": 4.89,
      "text": "Meanwhile the rest of the industry settled on a single shared plug."
    },
    {
      "id": "S18",
      "start": 105.302,
      "speech_end": 109.121,
      "end": 109.921,
      "dur": 4.619,
      "text": "Apple switched in 2023, with the iPhone 15."
    },
    {
      "id": "S19",
      "start": 109.921,
      "speech_end": 113.781,
      "end": 116.181,
      "dur": 6.26,
      "text": "The year after the European Union passed a law requiring it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S20",
      "start": 116.181,
      "speech_end": 118.091,
      "end": 118.891,
      "dur": 2.71,
      "text": "Now take something breaking."
    },
    {
      "id": "S21",
      "start": 118.891,
      "speech_end": 123.901,
      "end": 124.701,
      "dur": 5.81,
      "text": "Your screen cracks. You find the identical part from an identical phone."
    },
    {
      "id": "S22",
      "start": 124.701,
      "speech_end": 127.661,
      "end": 128.461,
      "dur": 3.76,
      "text": "You fit it. It works. Every pixel lights up."
    },
    {
      "id": "S23",
      "start": 128.461,
      "speech_end": 131.221,
      "end": 132.021,
      "dur": 3.56,
      "text": "And your phone tells you it doesn't recognise it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S24",
      "start": 132.021,
      "speech_end": 137.981,
      "end": 138.781,
      "dur": 6.76,
      "text": "The screen, the battery, the camera and the Face ID module each carry their own serial number."
    },
    {
      "id": "S25",
      "start": 138.781,
      "speech_end": 142.241,
      "end": 143.041,
      "dur": 4.26,
      "text": "That number is married to your logic board at the factory."
    },
    {
      "id": "S26",
      "start": 143.041,
      "speech_end": 145.151,
      "end": 145.951,
      "dur": 2.91,
      "text": "Swap the part, and the phone knows."
    },
    {
      "id": "S27",
      "start": 145.951,
      "speech_end": 150.411,
      "end": 151.211,
      "dur": 5.26,
      "text": "On the iPhone 13, changing a cracked screen stopped Face ID working."
    },
    {
      "id": "S27b",
      "start": 151.211,
      "speech_end": 153.081,
      "end": 155.681,
      "dur": 4.47,
      "text": "Not the screen. Face ID."
    },
    {
      "id": "S28",
      "start": 155.681,
      "speech_end": 158.091,
      "end": 158.891,
      "dur": 3.21,
      "text": "Fine, you think. Then I'll do it Apple's way."
    },
    {
      "id": "S29",
      "start": 158.891,
      "speech_end": 163.431,
      "end": 164.231,
      "dur": 5.34,
      "text": "Apple does run a programme that sends you the official parts and the official tools."
    },
    {
      "id": "S30",
      "start": 164.231,
      "speech_end": 167.241,
      "end": 168.041,
      "dur": 3.81,
      "text": "A journalist ordered it to change one battery."
    },
    {
      "id": "S31",
      "start": 168.041,
      "speech_end": 172.301,
      "end": 173.101,
      "dur": 5.06,
      "text": "It arrived as two flight cases weighing about thirty-six kilos."
    },
    {
      "id": "S32",
      "start": 173.101,
      "speech_end": 175.511,
      "end": 178.311,
      "dur": 5.21,
      "text": "The battery weighs about thirty grams."
    },
    {
      "id": "S33",
      "start": 178.311,
      "speech_end": 183.221,
      "end": 184.021,
      "dur": 5.71,
      "text": "Apple has since loosened this. Genuine used parts can now be paired."
    },
    {
      "id": "S34",
      "start": 184.021,
      "speech_end": 185.641,
      "end": 186.441,
      "dur": 2.42,
      "text": "Which is the interesting bit."
    },
    {
      "id": "S35",
      "start": 186.441,
      "speech_end": 190.951,
      "end": 193.551,
      "dur": 7.11,
      "text": "Not that it never changes. That it changes when somebody pushes."
    },
    {
      "id": "S36",
      "start": 193.551,
      "speech_end": 195.741,
      "end": 196.541,
      "dur": 2.99,
      "text": "Then there's the computer itself."
    },
    {
      "id": "S37",
      "start": 196.541,
      "speech_end": 204.073,
      "end": 204.873,
      "dur": 8.333,
      "text": "For decades, owning a computer meant you could open it. Add memory. Change a drive. Fit a better graphics card."
    },
    {
      "id": "S38",
      "start": 204.873,
      "speech_end": 207.813,
      "end": 208.613,
      "dur": 3.74,
      "text": "On a modern Mac, the memory is not a component."
    },
    {
      "id": "S39",
      "start": 208.613,
      "speech_end": 211.133,
      "end": 211.933,
      "dur": 3.32,
      "text": "It is packaged together with the processor."
    },
    {
      "id": "S40",
      "start": 211.933,
      "speech_end": 216.133,
      "end": 216.933,
      "dur": 5.0,
      "text": "There is no slot. There is no stick. There is nothing to open."
    },
    {
      "id": "S41",
      "start": 216.933,
      "speech_end": 222.473,
      "end": 223.273,
      "dur": 6.34,
      "text": "Which means the only moment you get to decide how much memory your computer will ever have..."
    },
    {
      "id": "S41b",
      "start": 223.273,
      "speech_end": 224.663,
      "end": 227.063,
      "dur": 3.79,
      "text": "...is before you buy it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S42",
      "start": 227.063,
      "speech_end": 229.073,
      "end": 229.873,
      "dur": 2.81,
      "text": "And it isn't only the hardware."
    },
    {
      "id": "S42b",
      "start": 229.873,
      "speech_end": 232.933,
      "end": 233.733,
      "dur": 3.86,
      "text": "On the Mac, you can still install whatever you like."
    },
    {
      "id": "S42c",
      "start": 233.733,
      "speech_end": 236.223,
      "end": 238.223,
      "dur": 4.49,
      "text": "On the phone, it's the door we started with."
    },
    {
      "id": "S43",
      "start": 238.223,
      "speech_end": 246.545,
      "end": 247.345,
      "dur": 9.122,
      "text": "A developer writes an iPhone app. Apple decides whether it reaches anybody at all, and the standard commission is thirty per cent."
    },
    {
      "id": "S45",
      "start": 247.345,
      "speech_end": 252.845,
      "end": 253.645,
      "dur": 6.3,
      "text": "So: you can't choose the shop. You can't choose the parts. You can't choose the memory."
    },
    {
      "id": "S45b",
      "start": 253.645,
      "speech_end": 255.155,
      "end": 257.955,
      "dur": 4.31,
      "text": "And all of it is yours."
    },
    {
      "id": "S46",
      "start": 257.955,
      "speech_end": 260.195,
      "end": 260.995,
      "dur": 3.04,
      "text": "Which brings us to the strangest one."
    },
    {
      "id": "S47",
      "start": 260.995,
      "speech_end": 266.835,
      "end": 267.635,
      "dur": 6.64,
      "text": "In 2016, people began noticing that their older iPhones were switching themselves off."
    },
    {
      "id": "S48",
      "start": 267.635,
      "speech_end": 272.045,
      "end": 272.845,
      "dur": 5.21,
      "text": "Not running out of charge. Switching off, with charge to spare."
    },
    {
      "id": "S49",
      "start": 272.845,
      "speech_end": 279.435,
      "end": 280.235,
      "dur": 7.39,
      "text": "There was a real reason for it. As a battery ages, it struggles to deliver a sudden burst of power."
    },
    {
      "id": "S50",
      "start": 280.235,
      "speech_end": 283.345,
      "end": 284.145,
      "dur": 3.91,
      "text": "So the phone would cut out in the middle of doing something."
    },
    {
      "id": "S51",
      "start": 284.145,
      "speech_end": 288.305,
      "end": 289.105,
      "dur": 4.96,
      "text": "Apple's fix was to slow the processor down before that could happen."
    },
    {
      "id": "S52",
      "start": 289.105,
      "speech_end": 292.445,
      "end": 293.245,
      "dur": 4.14,
      "text": "Which is, honestly, a sensible piece of engineering."
    },
    {
      "id": "S53",
      "start": 293.245,
      "speech_end": 295.755,
      "end": 296.555,
      "dur": 3.31,
      "text": "Apple shipped it in a software update."
    },
    {
      "id": "S53b",
      "start": 296.555,
      "speech_end": 298.965,
      "end": 301.365,
      "dur": 4.81,
      "text": "And didn't clearly say it slowed the phone."
    },
    {
      "id": "S54",
      "start": 301.365,
      "speech_end": 308.775,
      "end": 309.575,
      "dur": 8.21,
      "text": "For almost a year, millions of people had a phone that had been deliberately slowed. The notes mentioned power management."
    },
    {
      "id": "S55",
      "start": 309.575,
      "speech_end": 313.035,
      "end": 313.835,
      "dur": 4.26,
      "text": "It came out because somebody ran the numbers and published them."
    },
    {
      "id": "S56",
      "start": 313.835,
      "speech_end": 321.601,
      "end": 322.401,
      "dur": 8.565,
      "text": "Apple confirmed it, apologised, and for one year dropped the price of a replacement battery from seventy-nine dollars to twenty-nine."
    },
    {
      "id": "S57",
      "start": 322.401,
      "speech_end": 324.561,
      "end": 325.361,
      "dur": 2.96,
      "text": "The engineering was defensible."
    },
    {
      "id": "S57b",
      "start": 325.361,
      "speech_end": 326.921,
      "end": 329.921,
      "dur": 4.56,
      "text": "The communication wasn't."
    },
    {
      "id": "S58",
      "start": 329.921,
      "speech_end": 333.011,
      "end": 333.811,
      "dur": 3.89,
      "text": "Now here's the part that makes this genuinely hard."
    },
    {
      "id": "S59",
      "start": 333.811,
      "speech_end": 336.421,
      "end": 337.221,
      "dur": 3.41,
      "text": "Apple isn't doing any of this to annoy you."
    },
    {
      "id": "S60",
      "start": 337.221,
      "speech_end": 341.781,
      "end": 342.581,
      "dur": 5.36,
      "text": "Think about what actually happens when you take an Apple device out of its box."
    },
    {
      "id": "S61",
      "start": 342.581,
      "speech_end": 345.341,
      "end": 346.141,
      "dur": 3.56,
      "text": "Your headphones connect before you've asked them to."
    },
    {
      "id": "S62",
      "start": 346.141,
      "speech_end": 348.631,
      "end": 349.431,
      "dur": 3.29,
      "text": "Your photos are already on your laptop."
    },
    {
      "id": "S63",
      "start": 349.431,
      "speech_end": 352.771,
      "end": 353.571,
      "dur": 4.14,
      "text": "You copy something on one machine and paste it on another."
    },
    {
      "id": "S64",
      "start": 353.571,
      "speech_end": 355.781,
      "end": 356.581,
      "dur": 3.01,
      "text": "A phone call rings on your watch."
    },
    {
      "id": "S65",
      "start": 356.581,
      "speech_end": 358.071,
      "end": 358.871,
      "dur": 2.29,
      "text": "None of that is magic."
    },
    {
      "id": "S66",
      "start": 358.871,
      "speech_end": 363.011,
      "end": 365.411,
      "dur": 6.54,
      "text": "It works because Apple owns both ends of every one of those connections."
    },
    {
      "id": "S67",
      "start": 365.411,
      "speech_end": 368.921,
      "end": 369.721,
      "dur": 4.31,
      "text": "The same control that stops you fitting a screen you bought..."
    },
    {
      "id": "S67b",
      "start": 369.721,
      "speech_end": 371.831,
      "end": 374.631,
      "dur": 4.91,
      "text": "...is why the headphones just work."
    },
    {
      "id": "S68",
      "start": 374.631,
      "speech_end": 376.841,
      "end": 377.641,
      "dur": 3.01,
      "text": "Take one away and you take the other."
    },
    {
      "id": "S69",
      "start": 377.641,
      "speech_end": 380.801,
      "end": 381.601,
      "dur": 3.96,
      "text": "And this is why arguing about Apple goes nowhere."
    },
    {
      "id": "S70",
      "start": 381.601,
      "speech_end": 385.141,
      "end": 387.741,
      "dur": 6.14,
      "text": "Because the complaint and the compliment are about the same thing."
    },
    {
      "id": "S71",
      "start": 387.741,
      "speech_end": 390.901,
      "end": 391.701,
      "dur": 3.96,
      "text": "There's one more layer, and it isn't technical at all."
    },
    {
      "id": "S72",
      "start": 391.701,
      "speech_end": 396.991,
      "end": 397.791,
      "dur": 6.09,
      "text": "Apple doesn't just sell a device. It sells a way of thinking about technology."
    },
    {
      "id": "S73",
      "start": 397.791,
      "speech_end": 399.531,
      "end": 400.331,
      "dur": 2.54,
      "text": "Not: here is a telephone."
    },
    {
      "id": "S74",
      "start": 400.331,
      "speech_end": 404.813,
      "end": 407.013,
      "dur": 6.682,
      "text": "But: this changes everything. This is the future. Think different."
    },
    {
      "id": "S75",
      "start": 407.013,
      "speech_end": 410.673,
      "end": 411.473,
      "dur": 4.46,
      "text": "So people don't just own the thing. They tell you about it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S75b",
      "start": 411.473,
      "speech_end": 414.683,
      "end": 415.483,
      "dur": 4.01,
      "text": "Some critics say it behaves almost like a religion."
    },
    {
      "id": "S75c",
      "start": 415.483,
      "speech_end": 417.973,
      "end": 418.773,
      "dur": 3.29,
      "text": "Not literally. There are no Apple churches."
    },
    {
      "id": "S75d",
      "start": 418.773,
      "speech_end": 428.923,
      "end": 431.123,
      "dur": 12.35,
      "text": "But look at the shape of it. A founder with a legend attached. Events that happen every year. Believers. Sceptics. Arguments that never end."
    },
    {
      "id": "S76",
      "start": 431.123,
      "speech_end": 434.583,
      "end": 435.383,
      "dur": 4.26,
      "text": "Very few people describe their washing machine that way."
    },
    {
      "id": "S77",
      "start": 435.383,
      "speech_end": 437.843,
      "end": 438.643,
      "dur": 3.26,
      "text": "And that's where the real conflict starts."
    },
    {
      "id": "S78",
      "start": 438.643,
      "speech_end": 444.973,
      "end": 445.773,
      "dur": 7.13,
      "text": "Because \"think different\" comes from a company that is extremely specific about how you may use its products."
    },
    {
      "id": "S79",
      "start": 445.773,
      "speech_end": 447.683,
      "end": 448.483,
      "dur": 2.71,
      "text": "Which sounds like a contradiction."
    },
    {
      "id": "S79b",
      "start": 448.483,
      "speech_end": 449.511,
      "end": 451.911,
      "dur": 3.429,
      "text": "It isn't."
    },
    {
      "id": "S80",
      "start": 451.911,
      "speech_end": 453.971,
      "end": 454.771,
      "dur": 2.86,
      "text": "Apple isn't selling you freedom."
    },
    {
      "id": "S81",
      "start": 454.771,
      "speech_end": 458.331,
      "end": 459.131,
      "dur": 4.36,
      "text": "It's selling you a room where you never have to worry about anything."
    },
    {
      "id": "S82",
      "start": 459.131,
      "speech_end": 464.841,
      "end": 465.641,
      "dur": 6.51,
      "text": "Everything in it is placed well. Nothing is in your way. Nothing needs configuring."
    },
    {
      "id": "S83",
      "start": 465.641,
      "speech_end": 469.181,
      "end": 469.981,
      "dur": 4.34,
      "text": "And for millions of people, that is exactly what they want."
    },
    {
      "id": "S83b",
      "start": 469.981,
      "speech_end": 471.691,
      "end": 472.491,
      "dur": 2.51,
      "text": "You can move the furniture."
    },
    {
      "id": "S84",
      "start": 472.491,
      "speech_end": 474.691,
      "end": 475.491,
      "dur": 3.0,
      "text": "But if you want to move the walls..."
    },
    {
      "id": "S84b",
      "start": 475.491,
      "speech_end": 476.53,
      "end": 479.53,
      "dur": 4.039,
      "text": "...you can't."
    },
    {
      "id": "S84c",
      "start": 479.53,
      "speech_end": 483.42,
      "end": 484.22,
      "dur": 4.69,
      "text": "And Apple won't call that a wall. It'll call it design."
    },
    {
      "id": "S84d",
      "start": 484.22,
      "speech_end": 486.076,
      "end": 487.276,
      "dur": 3.056,
      "text": "You heard it earlier. Courage."
    },
    {
      "id": "S84e",
      "start": 487.276,
      "speech_end": 491.366,
      "end": 493.766,
      "dur": 6.49,
      "text": "So if it bothers you, there's nothing to report. There's only a preference."
    },
    {
      "id": "S85",
      "start": 493.766,
      "speech_end": 496.706,
      "end": 497.506,
      "dur": 3.74,
      "text": "Imagine two people buying the same computer."
    },
    {
      "id": "S86",
      "start": 497.506,
      "speech_end": 506.516,
      "end": 507.316,
      "dur": 9.81,
      "text": "The first one says: I don't want to configure anything. I don't want to spend Saturday fixing my own machine. I just want it to work."
    },
    {
      "id": "S86b",
      "start": 507.316,
      "speech_end": 509.626,
      "end": 510.426,
      "dur": 3.11,
      "text": "For that person, the room is a gift."
    },
    {
      "id": "S87",
      "start": 510.426,
      "speech_end": 517.681,
      "end": 518.481,
      "dur": 8.055,
      "text": "The second one says: I want to choose my own parts. I want to install what I like. I want to mend what I bought."
    },
    {
      "id": "S87b",
      "start": 518.481,
      "speech_end": 520.811,
      "end": 523.211,
      "dur": 4.73,
      "text": "For that person, the room is a cage."
    },
    {
      "id": "S88",
      "start": 523.211,
      "speech_end": 527.141,
      "end": 527.941,
      "dur": 4.73,
      "text": "And neither of them is wrong. They simply want different things."
    },
    {
      "id": "S88b",
      "start": 527.941,
      "speech_end": 534.861,
      "end": 535.661,
      "dur": 7.72,
      "text": "By the way, if you'd like to see where the next question takes us, consider subscribing. It really helps the channel."
    },
    {
      "id": "S89",
      "start": 535.661,
      "speech_end": 542.371,
      "end": 543.171,
      "dur": 7.51,
      "text": "So what is this argument actually about? Not Apple against Android. Not Mac against Windows."
    },
    {
      "id": "S89b",
      "start": 543.171,
      "speech_end": 545.481,
      "end": 548.481,
      "dur": 5.31,
      "text": "It's convenience against control."
    },
    {
      "id": "S90",
      "start": 548.481,
      "speech_end": 552.871,
      "end": 553.671,
      "dur": 5.19,
      "text": "Do you want to know how everything works? Or would you rather never have to?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S91",
      "start": 553.671,
      "speech_end": 556.831,
      "end": 557.631,
      "dur": 3.96,
      "text": "Apple is extremely good at offering you the second one."
    },
    {
      "id": "S91b",
      "start": 557.631,
      "speech_end": 563.531,
      "end": 565.931,
      "dur": 8.3,
      "text": "And that is exactly why millions of people love it, and exactly why some people can't stand it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S92",
      "start": 565.931,
      "speech_end": 571.741,
      "end": 572.541,
      "dur": 6.61,
      "text": "Apple doesn't just sell technology. It sells an idea about what technology should be."
    },
    {
      "id": "S93",
      "start": 572.541,
      "speech_end": 575.471,
      "end": 576.671,
      "dur": 4.13,
      "text": "And whether you love that idea or hate it..."
    },
    {
      "id": "S93b",
      "start": 576.671,
      "speech_end": 580.081,
      "end": 581.281,
      "dur": 4.61,
      "text": "...Apple has spent decades making sure you know what it is."
    }
  ]
}